1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,738
Your car door opens sideways,

2
00:00:02,738 --> 00:00:04,911
like a door in a house.

3
00:00:05,091 --> 00:00:07,738
A Lamborghini door goes straight up.

4
00:00:07,918 --> 00:00:11,080
A Mercedes from the nineteen fifties opens

5
00:00:11,080 --> 00:00:13,189
like the wings of a seagull.

6
00:00:13,369 --> 00:00:15,764
A McLaren door swings up and out

7
00:00:15,764 --> 00:00:17,037
like a butterfly.

8
00:00:17,217 --> 00:00:19,155
They look like showing off,

9
00:00:19,155 --> 00:00:21,308
but most of them started as an

10
00:00:21,308 --> 00:00:22,744
engineering problem.

11
00:00:22,924 --> 00:00:26,827
Today, ten parts of upward opening doors,

12
00:00:26,827 --> 00:00:29,112
and why each one exists.

13
00:00:29,461 --> 00:00:31,644
The basic problem is simple.

14
00:00:31,824 --> 00:00:33,825
A supercar is low,

15
00:00:33,825 --> 00:00:35,493
wide and stiff.

16
00:00:35,673 --> 00:00:38,238
The structure that makes it fast,

17
00:00:38,238 --> 00:00:41,191
a strong frame running along the sides

18
00:00:41,191 --> 00:00:42,201
of the cabin,

19
00:00:42,201 --> 00:00:44,144
also gets in the way of a

20
00:00:44,144 --> 00:00:45,077
normal door.

21
00:00:45,257 --> 00:00:47,742
And a long door that swings sideways

22
00:00:47,742 --> 00:00:49,674
needs a lot of space next to

23
00:00:49,674 --> 00:00:50,226
the car.

24
00:00:50,406 --> 00:00:53,424
Designers have found many different answers to

25
00:00:53,424 --> 00:00:54,539
that one problem.

26
00:00:54,889 --> 00:00:57,739
As always, every fact here comes from

27
00:00:57,739 --> 00:00:58,895
a named source,

28
00:00:58,895 --> 00:01:02,053
the car makers and automotive references,

29
00:01:02,053 --> 00:01:04,363
all listed in the description.

30
00:01:04,543 --> 00:01:06,842
Let's start with the most famous one.

31
00:01:07,191 --> 00:01:10,070
Why does a Lamborghini door go straight

32
00:01:10,070 --> 00:01:10,291
up?

33
00:01:10,471 --> 00:01:13,030
It started with the Countach in the

34
00:01:13,030 --> 00:01:14,419
nineteen seventies.

35
00:01:14,599 --> 00:01:17,061
The car was very wide and very

36
00:01:17,061 --> 00:01:20,016
low, with a wide structure along its

37
00:01:20,016 --> 00:01:20,508
sides.

38
00:01:20,688 --> 00:01:23,033
A normal door would have been long

39
00:01:23,033 --> 00:01:25,101
and heavy, and it would need a

40
00:01:25,101 --> 00:01:27,170
lot of space beside the car to

41
00:01:27,170 --> 00:01:27,515
open.

42
00:01:27,695 --> 00:01:30,099
A door that rotates upward,

43
00:01:30,099 --> 00:01:32,236
on a hinge at the front,

44
00:01:32,236 --> 00:01:35,442
needs almost no space beside the car

45
00:01:35,442 --> 00:01:36,066
at all.

46
00:01:36,415 --> 00:01:39,298
The idea came from the designer Marcello

47
00:01:39,298 --> 00:01:41,533
Gandini, who first used it on a

48
00:01:41,533 --> 00:01:44,055
concept car, the Alfa Romeo Carabo,

49
00:01:44,055 --> 00:01:45,785
in nineteen sixty-eight.

50
00:01:45,965 --> 00:01:48,268
On the Countach it also had a

51
00:01:48,268 --> 00:01:49,459
practical side.

52
00:01:49,639 --> 00:01:51,675
The rear view was so poor that

53
00:01:51,675 --> 00:01:54,592
drivers often reversed by opening the door,

54
00:01:54,592 --> 00:01:57,035
sitting on the sill and looking back

55
00:01:57,035 --> 00:01:57,917
over the car.

56
00:01:58,267 --> 00:01:59,819
After the Countach,

57
00:01:59,819 --> 00:02:03,492
scissor doors became a Lamborghini signature.

58
00:02:03,672 --> 00:02:05,941
The Diablo, the Murcielago,

59
00:02:05,941 --> 00:02:09,219
the Aventador and the Revuelto all have

60
00:02:09,219 --> 00:02:09,639
them.

61
00:02:09,819 --> 00:02:12,099
Today they are partly tradition,

62
00:02:12,099 --> 00:02:15,090
but they still solve the original problem.

63
00:02:15,270 --> 00:02:17,598
You can open a Lamborghini in a

64
00:02:17,598 --> 00:02:20,150
narrow parking space where a long,

65
00:02:20,150 --> 00:02:22,703
normal door would hit the car next

66
00:02:22,703 --> 00:02:23,154
to it.

67
00:02:23,503 --> 00:02:25,966
Why does the Mercedes three hundred S

68
00:02:25,966 --> 00:02:28,229
L have doors that open like wings?

69
00:02:28,409 --> 00:02:29,953
Because of its frame.

70
00:02:30,133 --> 00:02:32,323
The car was built on a light

71
00:02:32,323 --> 00:02:34,748
frame made of thin steel tubes,

72
00:02:34,748 --> 00:02:36,391
called a space frame.

73
00:02:36,571 --> 00:02:37,824
To make it stiff,

74
00:02:37,824 --> 00:02:40,331
the tubes ran high along the sides

75
00:02:40,331 --> 00:02:41,142
of the car,

76
00:02:41,142 --> 00:02:43,722
right where a normal door would be.

77
00:02:43,902 --> 00:02:46,208
There was simply no room for a

78
00:02:46,208 --> 00:02:47,130
normal door.

79
00:02:47,479 --> 00:02:49,952
The solution was to hinge the doors

80
00:02:49,952 --> 00:02:50,800
on the roof.

81
00:02:50,980 --> 00:02:52,127
When they open,

82
00:02:52,127 --> 00:02:54,496
they lift up and reveal a high,

83
00:02:54,496 --> 00:02:56,943
wide sill that the driver has to

84
00:02:56,943 --> 00:02:57,783
climb over.

85
00:02:57,963 --> 00:02:59,422
With both doors open,

86
00:02:59,422 --> 00:03:01,714
the car looks like a seagull with

87
00:03:01,714 --> 00:03:02,895
its wings raised,

88
00:03:02,895 --> 00:03:05,534
which is where the name gullwing comes

89
00:03:05,534 --> 00:03:05,881
from.

90
00:03:06,061 --> 00:03:09,715
The road car arrived in nineteen fifty-four,

91
00:03:09,715 --> 00:03:11,541
based on a racing car.

92
00:03:11,892 --> 00:03:13,378
Getting in was not easy.

93
00:03:13,558 --> 00:03:16,061
The steering wheel could even tilt out

94
00:03:16,061 --> 00:03:16,786
of the way,

95
00:03:16,786 --> 00:03:18,631
to help the driver climb in.

96
00:03:18,811 --> 00:03:19,942
But the stiff,

97
00:03:19,942 --> 00:03:22,366
light frame made the car fast,

98
00:03:22,366 --> 00:03:24,709
and the doors made it famous.

99
00:03:24,889 --> 00:03:27,233
More than fifty years later,

100
00:03:27,233 --> 00:03:30,664
Mercedes brought the gullwing back on the

101
00:03:30,664 --> 00:03:31,669
S L S A M G,

102
00:03:31,669 --> 00:03:34,096
as a tribute to the original.

103
00:03:34,446 --> 00:03:37,283
Why do McLaren doors swing up and

104
00:03:37,283 --> 00:03:39,519
out, like butterfly wings?

105
00:03:39,699 --> 00:03:41,839
Because they carry part of the roof

106
00:03:41,839 --> 00:03:42,451
with them.

107
00:03:42,631 --> 00:03:45,399
The hinge sits on the windscreen pillar,

108
00:03:45,399 --> 00:03:47,822
and the door rotates up and forward

109
00:03:47,822 --> 00:03:49,829
and outward at the same time.

110
00:03:50,009 --> 00:03:51,028
When it opens,

111
00:03:51,028 --> 00:03:53,067
it takes a piece of the roof

112
00:03:53,067 --> 00:03:55,688
along, leaving a big opening for the

113
00:03:55,688 --> 00:03:56,998
driver to step in.

114
00:03:57,348 --> 00:03:59,736
The McLaren F one road car of

115
00:03:59,736 --> 00:04:02,537
the nineteen nineties needed this.

116
00:04:02,717 --> 00:04:05,081
It had the driver in the centre,

117
00:04:05,081 --> 00:04:07,666
with a passenger seat on each side,

118
00:04:07,666 --> 00:04:08,847
slightly behind.

119
00:04:09,027 --> 00:04:10,787
To reach the middle seat,

120
00:04:10,787 --> 00:04:12,475
you need a huge opening.

121
00:04:12,655 --> 00:04:15,263
Butterfly doors that lift part of the

122
00:04:15,263 --> 00:04:17,448
roof make it possible to get in

123
00:04:17,448 --> 00:04:18,646
and slide across.

124
00:04:18,997 --> 00:04:22,271
Modern McLarens still use the idea.

125
00:04:22,451 --> 00:04:24,911
The carbon fibre cabin has high,

126
00:04:24,911 --> 00:04:27,680
strong sills, and the low roof would

127
00:04:27,680 --> 00:04:30,218
hit your head with a normal door.

128
00:04:30,398 --> 00:04:33,320
Opening upward and outward gives more room

129
00:04:33,320 --> 00:04:35,268
for your head and your legs,

130
00:04:35,268 --> 00:04:37,633
and it needs less space beside the

131
00:04:37,633 --> 00:04:39,581
car than a long normal door.

132
00:04:39,931 --> 00:04:42,754
Why does a Koenigsegg door rotate and

133
00:04:42,754 --> 00:04:45,120
swing forward at the same time?

134
00:04:45,300 --> 00:04:48,879
The company calls it the dihedral synchro

135
00:04:48,879 --> 00:04:49,840
helix door.

136
00:04:50,020 --> 00:04:50,935
As it opens,

137
00:04:50,935 --> 00:04:53,759
the door moves outward and then turns

138
00:04:53,759 --> 00:04:57,116
ninety degrees, standing upright next to the

139
00:04:57,116 --> 00:04:58,414
front of the car.

140
00:04:58,594 --> 00:05:00,377
It sounds complicated,

141
00:05:00,377 --> 00:05:03,214
but it solves two problems at once.

142
00:05:03,565 --> 00:05:05,948
First, the door moves out of the

143
00:05:05,948 --> 00:05:07,512
way of the high sill,

144
00:05:07,512 --> 00:05:09,300
so the opening is large.

145
00:05:09,480 --> 00:05:12,295
Second, it ends up standing beside the

146
00:05:12,295 --> 00:05:14,813
front wheel, not above the car and

147
00:05:14,813 --> 00:05:16,295
not far to the side.

148
00:05:16,475 --> 00:05:19,284
That means it needs little space around

149
00:05:19,284 --> 00:05:21,300
the car, and it does not hit

150
00:05:21,300 --> 00:05:23,317
a low ceiling in a garage or

151
00:05:23,317 --> 00:05:25,333
a high kerb beside the road.

152
00:05:25,684 --> 00:05:28,375
The mechanism is a precise piece of

153
00:05:28,375 --> 00:05:31,528
engineering, with a hinge that guides the

154
00:05:31,528 --> 00:05:33,451
door along a curved path.

155
00:05:33,631 --> 00:05:36,315
Koenigsegg uses it on all its cars,

156
00:05:36,315 --> 00:05:38,924
from the early models to the Jesko

157
00:05:38,924 --> 00:05:40,074
and the Gemera.

158
00:05:40,254 --> 00:05:42,288
It shows that even a door can

159
00:05:42,288 --> 00:05:45,164
become a showcase of the same engineering

160
00:05:45,164 --> 00:05:46,988
that goes into the engine.

161
00:05:47,338 --> 00:05:49,433
Why does the rear door of a

162
00:05:49,433 --> 00:05:51,761
Tesla Model X have two hinges?

163
00:05:51,941 --> 00:05:54,716
It is called a falcon wing door.

164
00:05:54,896 --> 00:05:57,289
A simple gullwing door on a tall

165
00:05:57,289 --> 00:05:59,534
car would swing far out to the

166
00:05:59,534 --> 00:06:00,805
side as it lifts.

167
00:06:00,985 --> 00:06:03,503
The falcon wing door has a hinge

168
00:06:03,503 --> 00:06:05,863
in the roof and a second hinge

169
00:06:05,863 --> 00:06:06,964
in the middle,

170
00:06:06,964 --> 00:06:08,852
so it folds as it rises,

171
00:06:08,852 --> 00:06:10,819
staying close to the car.

172
00:06:11,169 --> 00:06:12,608
According to Tesla,

173
00:06:12,608 --> 00:06:15,942
the door needs only about thirty centimetres

174
00:06:15,942 --> 00:06:18,367
of space beside the car to open.

175
00:06:18,547 --> 00:06:20,788
That makes it easier to get into

176
00:06:20,788 --> 00:06:23,099
the rear seats in a tight parking

177
00:06:23,099 --> 00:06:25,550
space, and it gives a tall opening,

178
00:06:25,550 --> 00:06:27,371
so you do not have to bend

179
00:06:27,371 --> 00:06:29,052
down to put a child in a

180
00:06:29,052 --> 00:06:29,402
seat.

181
00:06:29,582 --> 00:06:32,926
Sensors check for obstacles as it opens.

182
00:06:33,276 --> 00:06:34,961
It is not a supercar,

183
00:06:34,961 --> 00:06:37,049
but it uses the same idea.

184
00:06:37,229 --> 00:06:39,860
When there is little space beside the

185
00:06:39,860 --> 00:06:40,642
car, go up.

186
00:06:40,822 --> 00:06:42,715
The price is complexity.

187
00:06:42,895 --> 00:06:46,153
Two hinges, motors and sensors are more

188
00:06:46,153 --> 00:06:49,329
expensive and can go wrong more easily

189
00:06:49,329 --> 00:06:51,585
than a simple sliding door,

190
00:06:51,585 --> 00:06:54,509
which is why most family cars still

191
00:06:54,509 --> 00:06:55,178
use one.

192
00:06:55,528 --> 00:06:57,444
Why do you have to climb over

193
00:06:57,444 --> 00:06:59,294
such a high sill to get into

194
00:06:59,294 --> 00:07:00,021
a supercar?

195
00:07:00,201 --> 00:07:02,932
Because the sill is the backbone of

196
00:07:02,932 --> 00:07:03,556
the car.

197
00:07:03,736 --> 00:07:07,001
Most supercars are built around a tub,

198
00:07:07,001 --> 00:07:09,922
a stiff shell made of carbon fibre

199
00:07:09,922 --> 00:07:11,039
or aluminium.

200
00:07:11,219 --> 00:07:13,393
The thick sides of the tub run

201
00:07:13,393 --> 00:07:14,552
along the cabin,

202
00:07:14,552 --> 00:07:15,712
under the doors,

203
00:07:15,712 --> 00:07:17,741
and carry a lot of the car's

204
00:07:17,741 --> 00:07:18,394
strength.

205
00:07:18,744 --> 00:07:20,753
A stiff car handles better,

206
00:07:20,753 --> 00:07:23,507
because the suspension can do its job

207
00:07:23,507 --> 00:07:25,443
without the body twisting.

208
00:07:25,623 --> 00:07:28,750
And a tall side structure protects the

209
00:07:28,750 --> 00:07:31,219
people inside in a side crash.

210
00:07:31,399 --> 00:07:33,945
Making the sill lower would mean making

211
00:07:33,945 --> 00:07:35,381
it weaker, or heavier.

212
00:07:35,561 --> 00:07:37,819
So the engineers keep it high,

213
00:07:37,819 --> 00:07:40,077
and design the door around it.

214
00:07:40,427 --> 00:07:43,058
That is the real reason so many

215
00:07:43,058 --> 00:07:45,349
supercar doors open upward.

216
00:07:45,529 --> 00:07:47,623
A door that opens up takes part

217
00:07:47,623 --> 00:07:49,312
of the roof or the top of

218
00:07:49,312 --> 00:07:50,461
the sill with it,

219
00:07:50,461 --> 00:07:53,433
and makes the opening bigger without cutting

220
00:07:53,433 --> 00:07:55,595
into the strong structure below.

221
00:07:55,775 --> 00:07:58,478
The unusual door is the price of

222
00:07:58,478 --> 00:08:00,082
a stiff, light car.

223
00:08:00,433 --> 00:08:02,634
Why doesn't a heavy door that opens

224
00:08:02,634 --> 00:08:04,206
upward fall on your head?

225
00:08:04,386 --> 00:08:06,731
Because of the gas struts.

226
00:08:06,911 --> 00:08:09,664
A gas strut is a cylinder filled

227
00:08:09,664 --> 00:08:11,729
with gas under pressure.

228
00:08:11,909 --> 00:08:13,492
When the door opens,

229
00:08:13,492 --> 00:08:15,470
the gas pushes a rod out,

230
00:08:15,470 --> 00:08:18,082
and that push holds the weight of

231
00:08:18,082 --> 00:08:18,794
the door.

232
00:08:18,974 --> 00:08:21,178
It is the same part that holds

233
00:08:21,178 --> 00:08:23,161
up the boot lid on a normal

234
00:08:23,161 --> 00:08:23,455
car.

235
00:08:23,806 --> 00:08:26,250
On a door that opens sideways,

236
00:08:26,250 --> 00:08:28,612
gravity does not matter much.

237
00:08:28,792 --> 00:08:30,591
On a door that opens upward,

238
00:08:30,591 --> 00:08:32,582
the whole weight of the door is

239
00:08:32,582 --> 00:08:33,738
lifted every time.

240
00:08:33,918 --> 00:08:36,229
The struts are chosen so the force

241
00:08:36,229 --> 00:08:38,132
nearly balances that weight.

242
00:08:38,312 --> 00:08:40,083
The door feels light,

243
00:08:40,083 --> 00:08:42,107
rises with a small push,

244
00:08:42,107 --> 00:08:44,721
and stays open without a latch.

245
00:08:45,071 --> 00:08:47,926
The gas inside the struts is affected

246
00:08:47,926 --> 00:08:50,858
by temperature, and the seals wear out

247
00:08:50,858 --> 00:08:51,630
over time.

248
00:08:51,810 --> 00:08:52,989
On a cold day,

249
00:08:52,989 --> 00:08:55,514
a door may not rise as easily.

250
00:08:55,694 --> 00:08:56,792
On an old car,

251
00:08:56,792 --> 00:08:59,068
a worn strut can let the door

252
00:08:59,068 --> 00:08:59,931
drift down.

253
00:09:00,111 --> 00:09:02,417
That is why owners of cars with

254
00:09:02,417 --> 00:09:05,465
upward doors replace the struts as normal

255
00:09:05,465 --> 00:09:06,358
maintenance.

256
00:09:06,708 --> 00:09:08,499
Why does the door of a Ford

257
00:09:08,499 --> 00:09:09,958
G T cut into the roof?

258
00:09:10,138 --> 00:09:12,472
Because the car is so low.

259
00:09:12,652 --> 00:09:14,825
The original Ford G T forty,

260
00:09:14,825 --> 00:09:17,385
which won Le Mans in the nineteen

261
00:09:17,385 --> 00:09:20,644
sixties, was only about forty inches tall,

262
00:09:20,644 --> 00:09:21,963
around one metre.

263
00:09:22,143 --> 00:09:24,187
That is where its name comes from.

264
00:09:24,367 --> 00:09:25,863
With a roof that low,

265
00:09:25,863 --> 00:09:28,358
a normal door would leave almost no

266
00:09:28,358 --> 00:09:30,497
opening for the driver's head.

267
00:09:30,847 --> 00:09:33,458
So the door was extended into the

268
00:09:33,458 --> 00:09:33,854
roof.

269
00:09:34,034 --> 00:09:34,987
When it opens,

270
00:09:34,987 --> 00:09:36,961
it takes a large piece of the

271
00:09:36,961 --> 00:09:37,846
roof with it,

272
00:09:37,846 --> 00:09:39,888
and the driver can step in and

273
00:09:39,888 --> 00:09:41,998
lower themselves into the seat.

274
00:09:42,178 --> 00:09:44,956
In racing, this mattered even more,

275
00:09:44,956 --> 00:09:48,211
because drivers wear helmets and must get

276
00:09:48,211 --> 00:09:51,466
in and out quickly during driver changes.

277
00:09:51,816 --> 00:09:54,793
The modern Ford G T cars kept

278
00:09:54,793 --> 00:09:55,717
the idea.

279
00:09:55,897 --> 00:09:58,971
Many low race cars and supercars use

280
00:09:58,971 --> 00:10:01,876
doors that cut deep into the roof.

281
00:10:02,056 --> 00:10:03,902
It is the same lesson as the

282
00:10:03,902 --> 00:10:06,803
gullwing, approached from the top instead of

283
00:10:06,803 --> 00:10:07,396
the side.

284
00:10:07,576 --> 00:10:09,115
When the car is low,

285
00:10:09,115 --> 00:10:11,807
the door needs to borrow space from

286
00:10:11,807 --> 00:10:12,499
the roof.

287
00:10:12,849 --> 00:10:15,053
Why do the gullwing doors of the

288
00:10:15,053 --> 00:10:17,740
DeLorean have twisted metal bars in the

289
00:10:17,740 --> 00:10:18,085
roof?

290
00:10:18,265 --> 00:10:20,296
To lift heavy doors.

291
00:10:20,476 --> 00:10:23,606
The DeLorean was covered in stainless steel

292
00:10:23,606 --> 00:10:26,154
panels, which made the doors heavy.

293
00:10:26,334 --> 00:10:28,580
Gas struts alone could not lift them

294
00:10:28,580 --> 00:10:29,329
comfortably.

295
00:10:29,509 --> 00:10:32,229
So each door also has a torsion

296
00:10:32,229 --> 00:10:35,037
bar, a steel bar that is twisted

297
00:10:35,037 --> 00:10:36,879
when the door closes,

298
00:10:36,879 --> 00:10:39,424
and untwists to help lift it.

299
00:10:39,774 --> 00:10:42,402
The torsion bars were made with help

300
00:10:42,402 --> 00:10:45,761
from the aerospace company Grumman and treated

301
00:10:45,761 --> 00:10:47,076
with extreme cold,

302
00:10:47,076 --> 00:10:49,632
a process that helps the steel hold

303
00:10:49,632 --> 00:10:50,362
its shape.

304
00:10:50,542 --> 00:10:53,270
The bar stores energy like a spring.

305
00:10:53,450 --> 00:10:55,485
Together with gas struts,

306
00:10:55,485 --> 00:10:57,928
it lets a heavy door rise with

307
00:10:57,928 --> 00:11:00,126
a light push and stay open.

308
00:11:00,476 --> 00:11:02,734
Gullwing doors on a low car also

309
00:11:02,734 --> 00:11:05,345
need very little space beside the car

310
00:11:05,345 --> 00:11:05,909
to open.

311
00:11:06,089 --> 00:11:09,195
That is one reason the DeLorean became

312
00:11:09,195 --> 00:11:12,137
so memorable, along with its role in

313
00:11:12,137 --> 00:11:14,262
a famous time travel film.

314
00:11:14,442 --> 00:11:15,986
Behind the movie fame,

315
00:11:15,986 --> 00:11:18,231
the doors are a clever answer to

316
00:11:18,231 --> 00:11:19,353
a heavy problem.

317
00:11:19,704 --> 00:11:22,087
What happens if a car with gullwing

318
00:11:22,087 --> 00:11:23,721
doors lands on its roof?

319
00:11:23,901 --> 00:11:26,373
The doors are hinged to the roof,

320
00:11:26,373 --> 00:11:27,871
so they cannot open.

321
00:11:28,051 --> 00:11:30,408
The people inside could be trapped.

322
00:11:30,588 --> 00:11:31,998
That is a real risk,

323
00:11:31,998 --> 00:11:34,396
and it is the most serious problem

324
00:11:34,396 --> 00:11:36,370
with doors that open upward.

325
00:11:36,720 --> 00:11:39,469
Mercedes solved it on the S L

326
00:11:39,469 --> 00:11:42,124
S A M G with small explosive

327
00:11:42,124 --> 00:11:44,684
charges in the door hinges.

328
00:11:44,864 --> 00:11:47,378
If sensors detect that the car has

329
00:11:47,378 --> 00:11:50,483
rolled over, the charges fire and separate

330
00:11:50,483 --> 00:11:51,296
the hinges.

331
00:11:51,476 --> 00:11:53,709
The doors can then be pushed out

332
00:11:53,709 --> 00:11:56,290
and removed, so the people inside can

333
00:11:56,290 --> 00:11:58,802
get out, or rescuers can reach them.

334
00:11:59,152 --> 00:12:00,961
It is a good example of how

335
00:12:00,961 --> 00:12:03,575
every clever part creates a new problem

336
00:12:03,575 --> 00:12:05,653
that needs another clever part.

337
00:12:05,833 --> 00:12:08,357
The gullwing door solved the problem of

338
00:12:08,357 --> 00:12:09,328
the high frame.

339
00:12:09,508 --> 00:12:12,299
The explosive hinges solve the problem of

340
00:12:12,299 --> 00:12:13,525
the gullwing door.

341
00:12:13,705 --> 00:12:17,304
Engineering is often a chain of solutions.

342
00:12:17,654 --> 00:12:19,082
So here are the ten.

343
00:12:19,262 --> 00:12:21,606
Scissor doors for wide,

344
00:12:21,606 --> 00:12:22,524
low cars.

345
00:12:22,704 --> 00:12:25,432
Gullwings for a frame with no room.

346
00:12:25,612 --> 00:12:28,095
Butterfly doors that carry part of the

347
00:12:28,095 --> 00:12:28,422
roof.

348
00:12:28,602 --> 00:12:31,155
Rotating doors that stay out of the

349
00:12:31,155 --> 00:12:31,446
way.

350
00:12:31,626 --> 00:12:34,262
Falcon wings for tight spaces.

351
00:12:34,442 --> 00:12:36,896
A high sill that is the car's

352
00:12:36,896 --> 00:12:37,658
backbone.

353
00:12:37,838 --> 00:12:39,591
Struts that hold the weight.

354
00:12:39,771 --> 00:12:41,698
Roofs cut for helmets.

355
00:12:41,878 --> 00:12:44,223
Twisted bars for heavy steel.

356
00:12:44,403 --> 00:12:46,946
And explosive bolts for the worst day.

357
00:12:47,296 --> 00:12:49,860
A door that opens upward is not

358
00:12:49,860 --> 00:12:51,266
just showing off.

359
00:12:51,446 --> 00:12:53,590
It is the answer to a car

360
00:12:53,590 --> 00:12:54,618
that is low,

361
00:12:54,618 --> 00:12:55,904
wide and stiff.

362
00:12:56,084 --> 00:12:59,037
If you want more machines explained part

363
00:12:59,037 --> 00:13:01,843
by part, subscribe to Machine Reverse.

364
00:13:02,023 --> 00:13:04,046
And tell us in the comments which

365
00:13:04,046 --> 00:13:05,946
door you would want on your own

366
00:13:05,946 --> 00:13:06,191
car.
